riscv: dts: sophgo: sg2000: milkv-duos: enable USB in host mode

Enable the shared DWC2 USB controller on the Milk-V Duo S and pin it to
host mode. This board has a single USB2 port multiplexed between the
type-A host socket and the type-C device socket, so forcing host mode
here is necessary but not sufficient: routing the FSUSB30 data mux to the
type-A socket and enabling that socket's 5 V VBUS are done with two board
GPIOs in the follow-up patch 0029 (usb-host-mux-and-vbus). Without those,
a device on the type-A port does not enumerate even though the root hub
comes up.

Signed-off-by: d622 <300083818+d622-au@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duos.dts b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duos.dts
index ccccccc..ddddddd 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duos.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duos.dts
@@ -64,3 +64,8 @@
 &watchdog0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&usb {
+	dr_mode = "host";
+	status = "okay";
+};
